{"duration_api_ms":146180,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"66fc2e3d-de23-445d-b5ee-dcda5799252e","total_cost_usd":0.9885403999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56122,"cache_read_input_tokens":1222242,"output_tokens":14749,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2360},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56122,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1187,"cache_read_input_tokens":88123,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":337},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":14749,"cacheReadInputTokens":1222242,"cacheCreationInputTokens":56122,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9885403999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2360,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":56122,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":17,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I profiled all three client windows of the open-docx-10p journey on the integrated build. The per-module split in `.theseus/journeys/open-docx-10p.md` now comes from that profile instead of the PKT-0043 estimate. All six acceptance commands passed, `theseus scope-check` is clean, and the work is committed.\n\nThe packet asked for a quiet VM and I couldn't get one: the load average was about 5 during the run because other agents were working. The absolute times are inflated, so read the shares, not the milliseconds.\n\n**What I added:** `.theseus/oracle/journeys/open-docx-10p-profile.sh` and its runner `open-docx-10p-profile-run.cjs`. They run the same journey as `open-docx-10p.sh` (5 runs plus a warm-up, a new browser each time) while recording a CPU profile of the page. The editor iframe is on the same origin, so its work shows up in that profile. `attribute-word.js` then splits each window by module; it is unchanged.\n\n**Measured split** (share of CPU busy time, average per run):\n\n| window | busy ms | sdkjs-word | sdkjs-common | web-apps | browser |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| shell boot (goto → `asc_LoadDocument`) | 1 128 | 0 % | 5.8 % | 56.6 % | 37.7 % |\n| Editor.bin → load complete | 1 726 | 39.3 % | 14.9 % | 14.1 % | 31.6 % |\n| post-complete recalc | 684 | 38.3 % | 12.4 % | 24.4 % | 24.9 % |\n\n- **Compared with the old estimate:** word is about the same (39 % vs 41 %), common is lower (15 % vs 23 %) and the browser is higher (32 % vs 20 %).\n- **Idle time:** about 21 % of the Editor.bin → complete window is idle, waiting on fetches. It is now its own stage.\n- **Shell boot:** no word code runs there; it is all web-apps and the browser.\n- **Whole journey by module:** project (example service, nginx, browser, idle) 51.1 %, web-apps 20.8 %, sdkjs-word 12.7 %, docservice 6.5 %, sdkjs-common 5.3 %, x2t 3.6 %.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- I did not re-run the timing journey. Each window keeps its round-3 length and is split by the measured idle fraction and busy shares, so the stages still add up to 8 340 ms.\n- I added stages for each new module piece. The word recalc stage keeps the id `layout-finish-paint`, because `theseus validate` requires stage ids to be listed in `DIAG-sdkjs-word.md`.\n- The \"drawing & render\" bucket counts as sdkjs-word, but it also contains some common/Drawings code. Word is slightly overstated and common slightly understated; the map says so.\n\n**Not done:** the browser's largest item, 343 ms of `(program)` time, is not broken down further. That would need a full browser trace, not a CPU profile.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas** (also written in the packet):\n- The browser's network events carry both a monotonic time and a wall-clock time. That pair lets you place page marks on the CPU profile's timeline.\n- `attribute-word.js` can cut any time window if the profiles are named `open-<i>` and a `marks.json` gives each window's start and end.\n\nThe Executor log and friction line are filled in. The friction note is that nothing keeps other agents off the machine while a measurement packet runs.","ttft_ms":2791,"type":"result","duration_ms":1112292,"uuid":"3e383708-b3db-4898-ab99-a6cfd0dd0ae6","ttft_stream_ms":1865,"time_to_request_ms":212,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":101,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":6,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":19,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":108,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":126,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":211,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":219,"process_anon_mib_result":133,"process_peak_rss_mib":275,"process_cpu_ms_turn":15705,"process_wall_ms_turn":1112291,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1786,"process_wall_ms_streaming":111676,"main_stream_count":17,"main_stream_event_count":1969,"main_stream_chunk_count":1623,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_